  m_text: "A prefab is a GameObject kept as an asset, with its components and children. Each copy placed in a scene is an instance: the Hierarchy shows it with a blue cube icon. Change the prefab, and every instance changes with it.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> You open the Bench prefab and make its seat longer. What happens to the three benches here?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Double-click Bench in this sample's Prefabs folder to open it in Prefab Mode.\n2. Set the seat's Scale X to 1.5.\n3. Go back to the scene (the arrow at the top of the Hierarchy) and look at the benches.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Meshes topic, Liminal-Kit 3 \xB7 Columns and furniture (Bench)</color></size>"
