  m_text: "The Project window shows the assets: files in the Assets folder, such as meshes, materials and textures. A GameObject does not hold a copy of an asset; it points to it. Several objects can point to the same asset.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> The five crates share the material M_Crate. You change its colour. How many crates change?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select M_Crate in this sample's Materials folder.\n2. Change its Base Map colour.\n3. Select one crate and find M_Crate in its Mesh Renderer.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Materials topic, Materials-Training 1 \xB7 The material is an asset</color></size>"
