  m_text: "Importing copies a file into the project's Assets folder. Unity then makes an asset from it, with import settings shown in the Inspector, and writes a .meta file beside it that holds its ID. The original file stays where it was.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> You drag a photo from your desktop into the Project window, with the Imports folder open. Where does the new asset appear?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Open this sample's Imports folder in the Project window.\n2. Drag an image from your computer into it; select it and read its import settings.\n3. Right-click it \u203A Show in Explorer and find its .meta file.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Textures topic, Make-A-Material (phase 1, import)</color></size>"
